# CoffeeFlow — local secret store (TEMPLATE — no real values live in git)
#
# Install:   ./scripts/install-secrets.sh --link
# Real file: ~/.config/coffeeflow/secrets.env   (chmod 600, outside the repo)
#
# You only need to fill in the two BOOTSTRAP values below. Everything else lives
# encrypted in Supabase Vault and is fetched on demand:
#
#   . scripts/bootstrap-from-db.sh
#
# That way there is one place to rotate a credential — Vault — and a session
# started from your phone gets exactly the same set as a session on this Mac.
#
# This file is auto-loaded into every shell started inside the CoffeeFlow repo,
# so Claude Code sessions get it for free. Claude uses these by NAME ("$VAR")
# and never prints, cats or echoes the values.
#
# Rules:
#   - one KEY=value per line, no `export`; quote any value with a space or #
#   - a value here always beats Vault, which is handy for testing a rotation
#     before committing to it
#   - secrets that only edge functions read stay in `supabase secrets set`
#
# See what is loaded, without revealing any value:
#   ./scripts/secrets-doctor.sh --bootstrap

# ── BOOTSTRAP — the only two values that must live outside Vault ─────────────
# Production project. Both are also what a cloud session needs configured in its
# environment settings; nothing else has to be copied anywhere.
SUPABASE_URL=https://ytydgldyeygpzmlxvpvb.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Everything below is OPTIONAL on this machine ─────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to use Vault. Uncomment a line only to override Vault locally.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=        # sbp_… — Management API + CLI deploys
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=              # postgresql://postgres:<pw>@db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# WOO_URL=
# WOO_KEY=
# WOO_SECRET=
# META_SYSTEM_USER_TOKEN=
# META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=
# GOOGLE_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_CUSTOMER_ID=
# MFLOW_BASE=
# MFLOW_PUBLIC_KEY=
# MFLOW_SECRET_KEY=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
